-- title:
--   Independence Preserved By Almost-Everywhere Convergence
-- statement:
--   Let $m\leq m_\Omega$ be sigma-algebras on a probability space $(\Omega,P)$, and let $\mathcal X$ be a topological Borel space with closed-set outer approximation. Suppose $X_n:\Omega\to\mathcal X$ are measurable, $Y:\Omega\to\mathcal X$ is measurable, and $m$ is independent of the comap sigma-algebra of every $X_n$. If
--
--   $$X_n(\omega)\longrightarrow Y(\omega)$$
--
--   for $P$-almost every $\omega$, then $m$ is independent of the comap sigma-algebra generated by $Y$. The result transfers independence through an almost-everywhere pointwise limit and is useful for limiting constructions of random variables.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc/blob/984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932/LevyStochCalc/Probability/IndepLimit.lean#L54-L97 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `LevyStochCalc.Probability.IndepLimit`, declaration `LevyStochCalc.Probability.indep_comap_of_tendsto_ae`; the repository is private at upload time). Vendored from https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc at commit 984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932 (Apache-2.0; upstream copyright notice retained in the Lean text).

